# Keep the build context small and free of secrets.
#
# Mirrors the EXCLUDE list in tools/package.py: the zip and the image are two ways this
# working tree ships, and a pattern that is in one and not the other is a leak with a
# different delivery mechanism.
#
# Note the `**/` prefixes. Docker matches these patterns against the whole path from the
# context root and does NOT recurse on its own — bare `*.db` ignores `./forgecast.db` and
# happily copies `./forgecast/forgecast.db`. Since the Dockerfile does `COPY forgecast/`,
# every pattern that must hold at depth needs the prefix as well as the plain form.

# --- version control and CI -------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.github
.claude
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- environments and caches ------------------------------------------------------------
.venv
venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
.tox

# --- secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never ship a real .env into an image — the compose file mounts it at run time.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
# Private keys and certificates. The image gets its TLS trust from the base image's CA
# store, so any of these in the context is somebody's key, not a dependency.
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.cer
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
credentials.json
client_secret*.json
token.json
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/*.cer
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/credentials.json
**/client_secret*.json
**/token.json

# --- this machine's state ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The database and every SQLite sidecar. `-shm` and `-wal` hold database pages, so they
# are as sensitive as the database itself; `*.db` matches neither of them.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-journal
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
storage/
attachments/
runtime/
**/storage
**/attachments
**/runtime
# The operator's own scripting documents, if a copy ever lands in the tree. Somebody
# else's licensed work must not be baked into an image that gets pushed to a registry.
scripting-library*/
**/scripting-library*
*.log
**/*.log

# --- build output and development-only files --------------------------------------------
dist/
build/
**/node_modules
node_modules
remotion/out/
tests/
evidence.md
mirror.md
roadmap.md
